-7-779"><label>9.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rutten-van M&#x000f6;lken</surname><given-names>MP</given-names></name><name><surname>Oostenbrink</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Tashkin</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name><name><surname>Burkhart</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Monz</surname><given-names>BU</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Does quality of life of COPD patients as measured by the generic Euroquality of life five-dimension questionnaire differentiate between COPD severity stages?</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>2006</year><volume>130</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>1117</fpage><lpage>1128</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17035446</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b10-copd-7-779"><label>10.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DiBonaventura</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Paulose-Ram</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Su</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The impact of COPD on quality of life, productivity loss, and resource use among the elderly United States workforce</article-title><source>COPD</source><year>2012</year><volume>9</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>46</fpage><lpage>57</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">22292597</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="b11-copd-7-779"><label>11.</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DiBonaventura</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name><name><surname>Paulose-Ram</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Su</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The burden of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease among employed adults</article-title><so